(include-book "const-tail")

; L1, the CONST path's tail, part 2: the caller's branch chain at the run's
; states.
;
; The callee's dissolve leaves the comparison's value pushed into function
; 6's continuation INSIDE the CONST branch: the branch's own 13-instruction
; tail (const-rest), which uses (:LOCAL.SET 1) -- not the prologue's
; (:LOCAL.SET 0).  Every body below is spelled against that continuation
; (the quoted Q for the eqz's append, the const-rest/first-order spellings
; thereafter), with the pc substitution pc := (dadd pc) throughout.
;
; The eqz is conditional (the comparison is 1); the testop's result 0 then
; takes the else branch of the abort ifelse (the empty branch dissolves as
; a block and its label 0), and the fetch runs: global.get 1 (= (dadd pc)),
; the load (the operand word W), local.set 1, the second read, the add
; (pc := pc+4), the global.set 1 write, and the local.get 1 read-back.
;
; The ctxt facts below are the book's own recipes at the run's Z (the
; gset/frozen-store state and the frame-6 record) with the dadd substitution;
; the slice facts are proved at the state they are used at.  All of it is
; scratch-proven (tail109/110/112) and gathered here.

